// Six equal bars, 5:3, the proportion of the designer's 1000 by 600 pixel image.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "OSDD flag"
  designer "dexter (neopronouns on Tumblr)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2020-10-22"
  series "osdd-flag"
  version "original"
  design-rights "The designer's blog header says all of its edits are free to use, preferably with credit. This file's license covers the encoding, not the design."
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20220730124418/https://neopronouns.tumblr.com/post/632692357828050944/a-general-osdd-flag-can-be-used-to-represent-any"
  source "https://64.media.tumblr.com/37d30683683fbf836cc6d7c95e82d039/b74ca6e3959213ad-f6/s1280x1920/8232267d8954a2feb24d16e2801eb2ae77b79cc8.png"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20260104213042/https://pluralpedia.org/w/Other_Specified_Dissociative_Disorder"
  note "The designer, dexter of the Tumblr blog neopronouns, posted 'a general osdd flag! can be used to represent any of the subsets/types of osdd or osdd in general', inspired by three linked flags, on 22 October 2020 (Wayback Machine, 30 July 2022). The post gives no meanings or hex values."
  note "The colors are read from the post's flag image, 1000 by 600 pixels with six stripes of exactly 100: #fab067, #c2835a, #bdbdbd, #8462b8, #5d4f72 and #41005f. The 5:3 proportion is the image's. The post's second image is a banner, not a flag."
  note "Pluralpedia's main OSDD flag is a slightly tweaked version of this one by comet-queer, whose post (633514644342013952) couldn't be read. That version isn't encoded."
}
palette {
  orange "#fab067"
  brown "#c2835a"
  grey "#bdbdbd"
  purple "#8462b8"
  grey-purple "#5d4f72"
  dark-purple "#41005f"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars orange brown grey purple grey-purple dark-purple
